  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Halftone Field\n\nA flowing noise field printed as a grid of dots: each cell holds one dot whose size follows the field, so only the crests open up against the background, in a four-stop palette. A single WebGL fragment shader.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 10 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A moving dot-matrix backdrop behind a title: LED wall, music, tech or poster looks.\n- A palette-driven animated texture: four colour stops and a background decide the whole mood.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A calm, soft gradient is wanted: use shader-mesh-gradient.\n- The render budget is tight: the noise is evaluated for every pixel on the CPU, keep `resolution` at 0.75 or lower.\n\nVariables:\n- frequency (number, 1-10): Field frequency, default 2\n- speed (number, 0-10): Flow speed, default 5\n- cellSize (number, 1-100): Cell size, default 54\n- gamma (number, 1-20): Gamma (midtone crush), default 12\n- paletteBias (number, 0-20): Palette bias, default 2\n- palette1 (color): Palette stop 1 (lows), default \"#00aaff\"\n- palette2 (color): Palette stop 2, default \"#c2ff67\"\n- palette3 (color): Palette stop 3, default \"#6600ff\"\n- palette4 (color): Palette stop 4 (crests), default \"#000000\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#000000\"\n- quantize (boolean): Quantise to 30fps (stepped), default false\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: heygen-com/hyperframes. Licence: Apache-2.0. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Halftone Field\n\n  A flowing noise field printed as a grid of dots: each cell holds one dot whose size follows the field, so only the crests open up against the background, in a four-stop palette. A single WebGL fragment shader.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/bd6cff8157a1a0ed5075527e673cc4f321fe9123/registry/blocks/halftone-field/halftone-field.html\n\n  Copyright HeyGen, Inc. and the Hyperframes contributors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version\n  2.0 (the \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance with the License. You may obtain\n  a copy of the License at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Unless required by applicable\n  law or agreed to in writing, software distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\"\n  BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the License for\n  the specific language governing permissions and limitations under the License.\n\n  Changes by usemosio/blocks: fills the host frame instead of a fixed 1920×1080 scene, with the cell size scaled from the shorter side; the shader is WebGL2 (GLSL ES 3.0 syntax, otherwise unchanged); the canvas is drawn at the `resolution` variable and the clock comes from the timeline; without WebGL the background colour shows.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"halftone-field\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"10\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\": \"frequency\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Field frequency\", \"default\": 2, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 10, \"step\": 0.1},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Flow speed\", \"default\": 5, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 10, \"step\": 0.1},\n    {\"id\": \"cellSize\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Cell size\", \"description\": \"Dot spacing, relative to a 1080 px frame.\", \"default\": 54, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 100, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"gamma\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Gamma (midtone crush)\", \"default\": 12, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 20, \"step\": 0.1},\n    {\"id\": \"paletteBias\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Palette bias\", \"default\": 2, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 20, \"step\": 0.5},\n    {\"id\": \"palette1\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Palette stop 1 (lows)\", \"default\": \"#00aaff\"},\n    {\"id\": \"palette2\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Palette stop 2\", \"default\": \"#c2ff67\"},\n    {\"id\": \"palette3\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Palette stop 3\", \"default\": \"#6600ff\"},\n    {\"id\": \"palette4\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Palette stop 4 (crests)\", \"default\": \"#000000\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"default\": \"#000000\"},\n    {\"id\": \"quantize\", \"type\": \"boolean\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Quantise to 30fps (stepped)\", \"default\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up. Dots are fine, so 0.75 keeps them crisp.\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Halftone Field</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: #000;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .hlf-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .hlf-canvas {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"halftone-field\" data-duration=\"10\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"hlf-clip\" class=\"hlf-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"10\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"hlf-canvas\" class=\"hlf-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"halftone-field\";\n            var DUR = 10;\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"hlf-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function clampNum(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function hex(value, fallback) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(String(value || \"\").trim());\n              if (!m) return fallback;\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return \"#\" + h.toLowerCase();\n            }\n            function rgb(value) {\n              var h = hex(value, \"#000000\").slice(1);\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255];\n            }\n            var DEFS = [{\"id\": \"frequency\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Field frequency\", \"default\": 2, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 10, \"step\": 0.1}, {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Flow speed\", \"default\": 5, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 10, \"step\": 0.1}, {\"id\": \"cellSize\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Cell size\", \"description\": \"Dot spacing, relative to a 1080 px frame.\", \"default\": 54, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 100, \"step\": 1}, {\"id\": \"gamma\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Gamma (midtone crush)\", \"default\": 12, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 20, \"step\": 0.1}, {\"id\": \"paletteBias\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Palette bias\", \"default\": 2, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 20, \"step\": 0.5}, {\"id\": \"palette1\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Palette stop 1 (lows)\", \"default\": \"#00aaff\"}, {\"id\": \"palette2\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Palette stop 2\", \"default\": \"#c2ff67\"}, {\"id\": \"palette3\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Palette stop 3\", \"default\": \"#6600ff\"}, {\"id\": \"palette4\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Palette stop 4 (crests)\", \"default\": \"#000000\"}, {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"default\": \"#000000\"}, {\"id\": \"quantize\", \"type\": \"boolean\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Quantise to 30fps (stepped)\", \"default\": false}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up. Dots are fine, so 0.75 keeps them crisp.\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}];\n            var V = {};\n            DEFS.forEach(function (d) {\n              var raw = vars[d.id];\n              if (d.type === \"number\") V[d.id] = clampNum(raw, d.default, d.min, d.max);\n              else if (d.type === \"color\") V[d.id] = hex(raw, d.default);\n              else if (d.type === \"boolean\") V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"boolean\" ? raw : raw === \"true\" ? true : raw === \"false\" ? false : d.default;\n              else V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"string\" ? raw.trim() : d.default;\n            });\n\n            var W = Math.max(2, root.clientWidth);\n            var H = Math.max(2, root.clientHeight);\n            var cw = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * V.resolution));\n            var ch = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * V.resolution));\n            root.style.background = V.background;\n            canvas.width = cw;\n            canvas.height = ch;\n            function mapLinear(x, a1, a2, b1, b2) { return b1 + ((x - a1) * (b2 - b1)) / (a2 - a1); }\n            var PAL = [rgb(V.palette1), rgb(V.palette2), rgb(V.palette3), rgb(V.palette4)];\n            var BG = rgb(V.background);\n\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"in vec2 aPos;\",\n              \"out vec2 v_uv;\",\n              \"void main() { v_uv = vec2(aPos.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - aPos.y * 0.5); gl_Position = vec4(aPos, 0.0, 1.0); }\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n            var FRAGMENT = `#version 300 es\nprecision highp float;\nout vec4 outColor;\n\nuniform vec2 uRes;\nuniform float uTime;\nuniform float uFreq;\nuniform float uSpeed;\nuniform float uCell;\nuniform float uGamma;\nuniform float uBias;\nuniform vec3 uPal0;\nuniform vec3 uPal1;\nuniform vec3 uPal2;\nuniform vec3 uPal3;\nuniform vec3 uBg;\n\n// 3D simplex noise — Ashima Arts / Stefan Gustavson (MIT).\nvec3 mod289(vec3 x) { return x - floor(x * (1.0 / 289.0)) * 289.0; }\nvec4 mod289(vec4 x) { return x - floor(x * (1.0 / 289.0)) * 289.0; }\nvec4 permute(vec4 x) { return mod289(((x * 34.0) + 1.0) * x); }\nvec4 taylorInvSqrt(vec4 r) { return 1.79284291400159 - 0.85373472095314 * r; }\n\nfloat snoise(vec3 v) {\n  const vec2 C = vec2(1.0 / 6.0, 1.0 / 3.0);\n  const vec4 D = vec4(0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0);\n\n  vec3 i = floor(v + dot(v, C.yyy));\n  vec3 x0 = v - i + dot(i, C.xxx);\n\n  vec3 g = step(x0.yzx, x0.xyz);\n  vec3 l = 1.0 - g;\n  vec3 i1 = min(g.xyz, l.zxy);\n  vec3 i2 = max(g.xyz, l.zxy);\n\n  vec3 x1 = x0 - i1 + C.xxx;\n  vec3 x2 = x0 - i2 + C.yyy;\n  vec3 x3 = x0 - D.yyy;\n\n  i = mod289(i);\n  vec4 p = permute(permute(permute(\n      i.z + vec4(0.0, i1.z, i2.z, 1.0)) +\n      i.y + vec4(0.0, i1.y, i2.y, 1.0)) +\n      i.x + vec4(0.0, i1.x, i2.x, 1.0));\n\n  float n_ = 0.142857142857;\n  vec3 ns = n_ * D.wyz - D.xzx;\n\n  vec4 j = p - 49.0 * floor(p * ns.z * ns.z);\n\n  vec4 x_ = floor(j * ns.z);\n  vec4 y_ = floor(j - 7.0 * x_);\n\n  vec4 x = x_ * ns.x + ns.yyyy;\n  vec4 y = y_ * ns.x + ns.yyyy;\n  vec4 h = 1.0 - abs(x) - abs(y);\n\n  vec4 b0 = vec4(x.xy, y.xy);\n  vec4 b1 = vec4(x.zw, y.zw);\n\n  vec4 s0 = floor(b0) * 2.0 + 1.0;\n  vec4 s1 = floor(b1) * 2.0 + 1.0;\n  vec4 sh = -step(h, vec4(0.0));\n\n  vec4 a0 = b0.xzyw + s0.xzyw * sh.xxyy;\n  vec4 a1 = b1.xzyw + s1.xzyw * sh.zzww;\n\n  vec3 p0 = vec3(a0.xy, h.x);\n  vec3 p1 = vec3(a0.zw, h.y);\n  vec3 p2 = vec3(a1.xy, h.z);\n  vec3 p3 = vec3(a1.zw, h.w);\n\n  vec4 norm = taylorInvSqrt(vec4(dot(p0, p0), dot(p1, p1), dot(p2, p2), dot(p3, p3)));\n  p0 *= norm.x;\n  p1 *= norm.y;\n  p2 *= norm.z;\n  p3 *= norm.w;\n\n  vec4 m = max(0.6 - vec4(dot(x0, x0), dot(x1, x1), dot(x2, x2), dot(x3, x3)), 0.0);\n  m = m * m;\n  return 42.0 * dot(m * m, vec4(dot(p0, x0), dot(p1, x1), dot(p2, x2), dot(p3, x3)));\n}\n\n// Full-saturation, full-value HSV: only the hue ramp survives.\nvec3 hue2rgb(float h) {\n  return clamp(abs(mod(h * 6.0 + vec3(0.0, 4.0, 2.0), 6.0) - 3.0) - 1.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n}\n\n// Piecewise-linear ramp across the four palette stops.\nvec3 ramp(float v) {\n  float x = clamp(v, 0.0, 1.0) * 3.0;\n  vec3 c = mix(uPal0, uPal1, clamp(x, 0.0, 1.0));\n  c = mix(c, uPal2, clamp(x - 1.0, 0.0, 1.0));\n  c = mix(c, uPal3, clamp(x - 2.0, 0.0, 1.0));\n  return c;\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n  // One sample per cell, taken at the cell centre.\n  vec2 cell = floor(gl_FragCoord.xy / uCell);\n  vec2 centre = (cell + 0.5) * uCell;\n\n  vec2 st = centre / uRes;\n  st.x *= uRes.x / uRes.y;\n\n  float hue = abs(snoise(vec3(st * uFreq, uTime * uSpeed)));\n  vec3 field = hue2rgb(hue);\n\n  // The gamma is the whole look: it crushes the midtones so most of the frame\n  // stays background and only the crests of the field open up.\n  float gray = pow(dot(field, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722)), uGamma);\n  float v = clamp(gray + uBias, 0.0, 1.0);\n\n  float radius = v * 0.5 * uCell;\n  float d = length(gl_FragCoord.xy - centre);\n  float mask = 1.0 - smoothstep(radius - 1.0, radius + 1.0, d);\n\n  outColor = vec4(mix(uBg, ramp(v), mask), 1.0);\n}\n`;\n\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { alpha: false, antialias: false, depth: false, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var shader = gl.createShader(type);\n              gl.shaderSource(shader, source);\n              gl.compileShader(shader);\n              if (!gl.getShaderParameter(shader, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(shader) || \"shader compile failed\");\n              return shader;\n            }\n            var paint = null;\n            try {\n              if (!gl) throw new Error(\"WebGL2 is not available\");\n              var prog = gl.createProgram();\n              gl.attachShader(prog, compile(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERTEX));\n              gl.attachShader(prog, compile(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAGMENT));\n              gl.bindAttribLocation(prog, 0, \"aPos\");\n              gl.linkProgram(prog);\n              if (!gl.getProgramParameter(prog, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(prog) || \"link failed\");\n              gl.useProgram(prog);\n              var buffer = gl.createBuffer();\n              gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buffer);\n              gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 3, -1, -1, 3]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n              gl.enableVertexAttribArray(0);\n              gl.vertexAttribPointer(0, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);\n              gl.viewport(0, 0, cw, ch);\n              function u(name) { return gl.getUniformLocation(prog, name); }\n              gl.uniform2f(u(\"uRes\"), cw, ch);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"uFreq\"), mapLinear(V.frequency, 1, 10, 0.3, 6));\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"uSpeed\"), V.speed * 0.05);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"uCell\"), mapLinear(V.cellSize, 1, 100, 6, 60) * Math.min(cw, ch) / 1080);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"uGamma\"), mapLinear(V.gamma, 1, 20, 0.5, 8));\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"uBias\"), V.paletteBias * 0.05);\n              PAL.forEach(function (c, i) { gl.uniform3f(u(\"uPal\" + i), c[0], c[1], c[2]); });\n              gl.uniform3f(u(\"uBg\"), BG[0], BG[1], BG[2]);\n              var timeLoc = u(\"uTime\");\n              paint = function (t) {\n                gl.uniform1f(timeLoc, V.quantize ? Math.floor(t * 30) / 30 : t);\n                gl.clearColor(0, 0, 0, 0);\n                gl.clear(gl.COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);\n                gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLES, 0, 3);\n              };\n            } catch (err) {\n              canvas.style.display = \"none\";\n              if (window.console) console.warn(NAME + \":\", err.message);\n            }\n\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true, onUpdate: function () { if (paint) paint(tl.time()); } });\n\n            // The block lasts DUR seconds even when nothing is tweened at the end.\n            tl.set({}, {}, DUR);\n            if (paint) paint(0);\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
